From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:45:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] JavaScript: Window events, uncaught errors, timer ids and
 binding fixes

- DOMContentLoaded reaches the Window's listeners (it bubbles there from
  the Document); events NetSurf dispatches at the Window have the
  Window as currentTarget and, without a libdom target, as target; the
  target of load and DOMContentLoaded at the Window is the Document.
- Errors thrown in event listeners were logged at DEBUG level and
  promises rejected without a handler were dropped by the QuickJS
  layer; both are reported as uncaught errors now.
- Timer handles start at 1: clearTimeout(0) cancelled the first timer.
- The running script element is recorded (html_script.node,
  current_script) for document.currentScript; external scripts' elements
  get the load event after running and the error event when the fetch
  fails (script loaders wait for them).
- createComment and createProcessingInstruction; template elements
  get HTMLTemplateElement's prototype, doctypes DocumentType's, CDATA
  sections Text's; classList.value of an element without class read a
  NULL string.
